// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// UI Generator / Editor — Deno Edge Function (v2 — Slot-Based Architecture)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Generates SwiftUI component JSON for a native iOS app that renders it.
//
// v2 removes the fixed molecule/organism registry and deterministic renderers.
// Instead, each screen section ("slot") is generated by the LLM with structural
// constraints, producing unique layouts per app theme while remaining schema-safe.
//
// Architecture (full-canvas generation):
//
//   Prompt
//     │
//     ├─► classifyArchetype  ──────► ScreenArchetype (dashboard, feed, …)
//     │
//     ├─► extractThemeTokens  ─────► ThemeTokens (appName, tone, accent, …)
//     │                               (includes sharedFacts for cross-slot consistency)
//     │
//     ├─► planSlots  ──────────────► SlotPlan[] (ordered slot types + intents)
//     │                                (informed by archetype + theme)
//     ▼
//   For each slot in parallel:
//     │
//     ├─► retrieveExemplars (pgvector)  ──► 2-3 full component-tree examples
//     │                                     for THIS slot type × domain
//     ▼
//     └─► generateSlot (LLM)  ────────────► AnyComponent subtree
//                                            constrained by slot rules + theme
//     │
//     ├─► validateSlot  ──────────────────► structural constraint check
//     │     (fail? → repair with specific issues, up to 2 retries)
//     ▼
//     └─► postProcessComponents  ─────────► schema normalization
//
//   assembleScreen  ──────────────────────► final screen tree
//
// Selection editing path is UNCHANGED from v1.
//
// Slot Types (broad, composable — not a fixed visual template):
//   app_header, hero_banner, stat_group, content_list, content_grid,
//   horizontal_rail, action_bar, nav_bar, section_header, media_player,
//   profile_header, form_section, empty_state, banner_alert, segmented_tabs,
//   timeline_list, settings_list, chart_section, social_feed, gallery_grid,
//   onboarding_step, search_bar, fab_button, card_detail, pricing_table,
//   calendar_strip, progress_section, testimonial_rail, feature_grid,
//   comparison_table, countdown_timer, weather_widget, map_preview,
//   notification_list, chat_bubble_list, story_rail, avatar_group,
//   breadcrumb_nav, split_view, floating_card
//
// The LLM writes SwiftUI JSON directly for each slot, but within tight
// structural constraints (max depth, required elements, allowed roots).
// This is the core shift from v1: variety comes from the LLM's layout
// creativity, safety comes from per-slot validation + repair.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

